Z||000002||Patrick's Dad||05-13-2001||03:32 PM||||The first one was actually done by a station owner in MN, I think. I saw it on the news a couple of days ago. The 89 octane was "ARM" and the 92 was "LEG."<P>I remember back during the seventies (wait, let me get my cane) seeing a comic where the guy says to the pump jockey, "Fill it up or twenty five dollars, whichever comes first." I'm surprised they haven't re-issued that one, with a hundred dollar limit....||||reg||1
